tooltip.rsaudio.loader.1=Pastes a structure from config/rsaudio/structures into the world
tooltip.rsaudio.loader.2=Right-click to pick a structure, set the offset and press Load
tooltip.rsaudio.loader.3=Sneak + right-click loads once with the current settings
tooltip.rsaudio.loader.4=A redstone rising edge loads once too, so it can build automatically
tooltip.rsaudio.computer.1=Run a tiny assembly program that drives the redstone output of all six faces
tooltip.rsaudio.computer.2=Right-click to open the editor and press Run; each face outputs 0-15 independently
tooltip.rsaudio.computer.3=Read any face as input to build blinkers, pulse trains and telegraphs
tooltip.rsaudio.computer.4=Sneak + right-click toggles run/stop
tooltip.rsaudio.alarm.1=Lights up when powered by redstone, and can flash
tooltip.rsaudio.alarm.2=Right-click to set the flash period and the buzzer
tooltip.rsaudio.alarm.3=Sneak + right-click toggles the buzzer
tooltip.rsaudio.door.1=A configurable sliding door whose blast resistance is in another league (survives nukes)
tooltip.rsaudio.door.2=Right-click with a wooden axe to open/close (bare hands do nothing); sneak + right-click for settings, set width/height/facing then press Build
tooltip.rsaudio.door.3=Panels grow to the right of the facing and upwards; the controller is always the bottom-left block
tooltip.rsaudio.door.4=A redstone signal opens it; it waits for entities to leave before closing, so nobody gets crushed
tooltip.rsaudio.door.5="Lock" means a FAAS remote lockdown: nothing local can open it (closing is always allowed, so a lockdown never leaves a gap)
tooltip.rsaudio.door.6=Doors on the same channel are interlocked: while one is open the other cannot open, and after one closes the other side must wait out the cycle time. Two facing doors on one channel make an airlock
tooltip.rsaudio.door.7=Turn on "Heavy": the door rises row by row, one row every "stage" ticks, like a huge armoured gate. (Tartarus is separate: a circular hatch door, its own block)

