tooltip.rsaudio.elevator_controller_freight.2=Placed like the passenger type: one shaft column plus a controller mounted against it
tooltip.rsaudio.elevator_controller_freight.3=Car is 5x3 and carries up to 24 cells; it travels slower and holds the door open longer (loading takes time)
tooltip.rsaudio.elevator_controller_freight.4=Leave a 5x3 shaft clearance - too narrow and the car jams against the shaft wall and reports "shaft blocked"

tooltip.rsaudio.elevator_controller_inclined.1=Inclined elevator controller: the shaft rises and shifts sideways at the same time (like a minecart ramp)
tooltip.rsaudio.elevator_controller_inclined.2=How to place: shift the shaft one block to the same side on every level, and mount the controller at the starting level
tooltip.rsaudio.elevator_controller_inclined.3=The car always stays level (it does not tilt with the shaft) and can serve up to 32 floors
tooltip.rsaudio.elevator_controller_inclined.4=The GUI states the horizontal shift direction; if it does not match the shaft you get "no shaft"

